      "url": "https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320842/20260717/chip-design-agents-move-foundry-cadence-innostack-joins-rapidus-2nm-node.htm",
      "summary": "Chip Design Agents Move Into Foundry: Cadence InnoStack Joins Rapidus 2nm Node Tech Times",
      "body": "Chip designers evaluating Japan's Rapidus 2nm foundry will now get something no other advanced-node fab has bundled into its process design kit: a full agentic AI design orchestration layer, courtesy of Cadence's InnoStack AI Super Agent. Rapidus and Cadence announced the collaboration on Thursday, integrating InnoStack into the Rapidus AI-Agentic Design Solution (Raads) platform that ships with Rapidus's 2nm process design kit. The stated target is up to a 2× improvement in design turnaround time over conventional back-end flows — a claim that has not been independently validated but that, if realized, would meaningfully change the calculus of whether to route an advanced SoC project through a brand-new foundry.\nThe partnership is the first documented deployment of Cadence's InnoStack agent inside a foundry's customer-facing design environment, and it arrives at a strategically sensitive moment: Rapidus is trying to convert more than 60 active customer discussions into binding volume ",
